# The API's *internal* address, used server-side by the Next.js rewrites.
# Browser code never calls it — it stays same-origin at /api/* — so this URL
# must be reachable from the dashboard process, not from the user's machine.
#
#   local       http://localhost:4000
#   staging     https://api-staging.reygent.com
#   production  https://api.reygent.com
API_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:4000

# There is deliberately no "dashboard URL" variable: the dashboard is
# host-agnostic and works under any name a reverse proxy gives it
# (oms.reygent.com in development, app.reygent.com or similar in production).
# Only the API needs a public identity, because Shopify stores that URI:
#   APP_URL=https://oms.reygent.com   → webhooks hit <APP_URL>/webhooks/shopify,
#                                       which this server forwards to the API
#   APP_URL=https://api.reygent.com   → webhooks go straight to the API host
# See "Hosts and origins" in docs/SHOPIFY-CONNECT.md.
